---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
const updated = 'July 2026'
---
<Layout title="Cookie Policy — QuoteLens" description="How QuoteLens uses cookies.">

  <section class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">QuoteLens</p>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteLens uses only the cookies it needs to work, plus optional
      analytics cookies you can accept or decline. We do not use
      advertising cookies, and we do not sell what we collect.
    </p>

    <h2>What we use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Session cookies</strong> — set when a business signs in to
        its dashboard, so you stay signed in. These are strictly necessary;
        without them you could not log in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics (Google Analytics)</strong> — helps us understand
        how visitors use QuoteLens, such as which pages are viewed and how
        people arrive at the site. These cookies are not set until you
        accept them in the cookie banner shown on your first visit — you
        can decline, and QuoteLens works exactly the same either way.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Customers getting a quote</h2>
    <p>
      If you are using a business's quote link, you do not need an account
      and we do not set a login cookie for you.
    </p>

    <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Your browser can block or delete cookies. Blocking the session cookie
      will prevent businesses from signing in to the dashboard. You can
      also change your analytics choice at any time by clearing your
      browser's site data for quote-lens.app, which will show the cookie
      banner again on your next visit.
    </p>

    <h2>More</h2>
    <p>
      See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle
      personal data generally.
    </p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to QuoteLens</a></p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>